 "notes": [
  "Breadboard hole positions are estimated from the circuit image. The photoresistor straddles the centre gap at column 21; the 100 ohm resistor straddles it at column 9.",
  "The 4.7K resistor is placed from 21b.c to 24b.c so it shares the A0 node with the photoresistor's lower leg. The black GND wire lands in column 24 (24b.b).",
  "The speaker's black lead goes straight to the Arduino's digital-header GND (modelled as GND.3). Its red lead goes into 9t.g, the same strip as the 100 ohm resistor. The speaker wires are assumed to be pin-ended leads.",
  "The 100 ohm resistor sits between pin 9 and the speaker. The tutorial's schematic labels it 10K, but the text and parts list say 100 ohm, so 100 ohm is used.",
  "The power GND wire uses GND.2, one of the two GND pins on the power header."
